body:
An overlay repository should automate an upstream repository without forking it. The overlay holds only `.smithers/`; its `.smithers/config.ts` default-exports `S.Mounts({ <name>: S.Mount({ repository, ref, track?, drift?, patches?, overlay? }) })`.

Every build-CLI command run from the overlay materializes the mount before it plans:

1. read `track` with `git ls-remote` and apply the drift policy (`warn`, `refuse`, `follow`);
2. fetch the pinned commit into `.mounts/<name>` and check it out detached;
3. apply the declared patches as commits on the pin;
4. lay the overlay's `.smithers/` over the checkout;
5. plan against the checkout, so `//` labels and upstream configs resolve as if the overlay lived upstream.

Upstream is only read. Edits in the checkout, edits to a laid file, and overlay files that collide with tracked upstream files are refused rather than discarded.

First consumer: an overlay that mounts Effect 4 (Effect-TS/effect main) and runs `packages/effect` typecheck, tests, oxlint, and an agent lane over Effect's own written conventions.

Design: `packages/smithers/build/build-cli/docs/concepts/mounts.md`.
